.bd
SUBROUTINE
.in +5
.br
.bd
strcat
- concatenate two strings
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
C
.in +5
.br
.bd 3
char *strcat(s1, s2)
char *s1;
char *s2;
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
FUNCTION
.in +5
.br
strcat appends a copy of s2 to the end of s1.  The first
character of s2 overwrites the terminating null of s1.

s1 must point to a region large enough to hold both strings
and the terminating null.
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
RETURNS
.in +5
.br
s1, the destination string.
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
